    "finding": "For PR #3066, default-five-worker strict linkcheck took about 133 seconds with four rate-limit waits across three existing GitHub URLs. The corresponding exact-main run took about 254 seconds with three waits on demos/README.md. Both strict builds succeeded. The two-worker retention criterion from sequence 986 is not met for this default-worker baseline (target is at most 120 seconds and one wait per run). The workflow triggers are distinct candidate and landed-source validations; no duplicate invocation, coverage, retry, timeout, warning, or failure semantics were changed. The paired evidence confirms recurring external rate-limit latency and its variability; it does not isolate worker count as the cause.",
